{
  "ruleId": "DED-SPECIFIED-DISEASE",
  "_note": "Treatment of a specified disease: s.128(1): a resident assessee, \"the amount actually paid during the tax year or a sum of ₹ 40000, whichever is less … for the medical treatment of such disease or ailment as may be prescribed — (a) for himself or a dependant\" (p.164); \"reduced by any amount received under an insurance from an insurer, or reimbursed by an employer\" (s.128(3), p.165); the prescribed disease and specialist's prescription (s.128(1)–(2)) are entry conditions; \"dependant\" as s.127(9) (s.128(5)(a)). ChapterEightNode allows the lesser of (paid − reimbursed) and this limit. rulebook DED-80DDB-001. Old regime only (s.202(2)(a)(xii), p.227). TY 2026-27 only; the 1961 counterpart, s.80DDB, is unread (W-075d). D-138.",
